1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,587
What is the difference between paying ten dollars with cash... and ten dollars with card?

2
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:05,937
Same ten dollars.

3
00:00:05,937 --> 00:00:06,825
For Doug.

4
00:00:06,825 --> 00:00:08,012
But not for Puffin.

5
00:00:08,012 --> 00:00:09,062
This is Doug.

6
00:00:09,062 --> 00:00:10,587
Doug have three hairs.

7
00:00:10,587 --> 00:00:11,800
Doug need haircut.

8
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:13,312
Puffin cut Doug hair.

9
00:00:13,312 --> 00:00:14,825
Doug pay ten dollars.

10
00:00:14,825 --> 00:00:15,637
Cash.

11
00:00:15,637 --> 00:00:17,650
Puffin keep all ten dollars.

12
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:19,862
Next week, Doug pay with card.

13
00:00:19,862 --> 00:00:20,550
Beep.

14
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:23,000
Puffin get nine dollars seventy-six.

15
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,462
Twenty-four cents is the swipe fee.

16
00:00:25,462 --> 00:00:27,975
It go to the card bank and the card network.

17
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:29,125
Fox the Banker.

18
00:00:29,125 --> 00:00:30,262
Is Fox lazy?

19
00:00:30,262 --> 00:00:30,950
No.

20
00:00:30,950 --> 00:00:32,350
Fox stop thieves.

21
00:00:32,350 --> 00:00:34,662
Fox give money back if card is stolen.

22
00:00:34,662 --> 00:00:36,837
Fox let Doug buy now, pay later.

23
00:00:36,837 --> 00:00:39,325
So Puffin pay a little for every beep.

24
00:00:39,325 --> 00:00:40,775
But Puffin is smart.

25
00:00:40,775 --> 00:00:42,662
Puffin raise the haircut price.

26
00:00:42,662 --> 00:00:43,675
For everybody.

27
00:00:43,675 --> 00:00:44,812
Cash people too.

28
00:00:44,812 --> 00:00:45,487
Doug.

29
00:00:45,487 --> 00:00:47,162
And card people get points.

30
00:00:47,162 --> 00:00:48,175
Cash back.

31
00:00:48,175 --> 00:00:49,300
Little gifts.

32
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:50,675
Who pay for the gifts?

33
00:00:50,675 --> 00:00:52,425
Partly... the cash people.

34
00:00:52,425 --> 00:00:59,237
In real life, American stores paid one hundred ninety-eight billion dollars in swipe fees in twenty twenty-five.

35
00:00:59,237 --> 00:01:03,875
And Federal Reserve researchers found cash payers help pay for card rewards.

36
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:05,150
Card is not evil.

37
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:06,537
Cash is not magic.

38
00:01:06,537 --> 00:01:08,612
Cash: no fee for Puffin.

39
00:01:08,612 --> 00:01:10,987
Card: safe and fast for Doug.

40
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:12,262
Cash or card?

41
00:01:12,262 --> 00:01:13,437
Which one you use?

42
00:01:13,437 --> 00:01:15,087
Tell Doug in the comments.

